{
  "_about": "Per-control ride-live map, MEASURED on this rig by fxprobe.py (2026-09-03): sweep each control through the real jalv+FIFO path while a tone runs through, score transients. 'ride' = smooth to sweep during performance; 'set' = clicks/zippers, set it while parked. LV2 control ports step once per audio block, so the host CANNOT smooth 'set' controls by writing faster -- the fix for dry/wet + level is an audio-rate host mix (see AUDIO_HOST_SPLIT / fx notes). Reverb size/decay is intrinsically un-rideable. Unprobed keepers (purestdrive, baxandall, Equalizer8Band, Compressor) are omitted until measured.",
